## Contract (raw bpy module; the harness builds it once and the zones instance it)
{{ frame_doc }}
{{ asset_contract }}
- `{{ asset_file }}` must define `def build_{{ asset_file.rsplit('/', 1)[-1][:-3] }}(ctx, variant=0)` that links
  every part into `ctx.collection` (its own Collection, pre-made and active) and returns it: built at
  the origin, lowest point on z = 0, footprint centred on the origin, front facing −Y, sized as stated
  (the check errors beyond 2.5 × or under 0.4 × on any axis; zones instance it at scale 1).  Zone code places collection instances of `ctx.assets['{{ asset_file.rsplit('/', 1)[-1][:-3] }}']` by
  that origin and never calls you.
- Procedural mesh built in code (bmesh or `from_pydata`, any construction); every part carries a
  Principled material with a real colour and roughness (`Base Color`, `Roughness`, `Metallic`), varied at
  more than one scale (broad tone and wear plus fine grain or bump) where the real material varies.
  Objects are uniquely named PascalCase: one root mesh, or children parented under it at RELATIVE
  locations.  No harness library ships in this scene: every part is raw `bpy` / `bmesh` / `mathutils`
  written in this file (an import of `lib` is a lint ERROR), and the module is self-contained.
- A natural thing has an organic silhouette (judged): a tree is a trunk branching into limbs that carry
  leaf or needle cards, a rock an irregular asymmetric mass — never a cone, a ball on a stick or a cube
  standing in for one.
- `variant` (0..n) and `ctx.rng(seed)` may vary details deterministically; `random.*` is a lint error.
- At most 15000 triangles for the whole asset (it is instanced; the census counts them).
- No lights, no cameras, no world, no file IO; the lint warns on `bpy.ops.mesh.primitive_*` in a loop;
  nothing outside the asset itself (no ground plane).
- MOTION (only when the description names a moving part — a swinging lamp, a turning wheel): keyframe
  that part's OWN rotation/location on `ctx.frame(0.0)` and `ctx.frame(1.5)` (LINEAR, set on the slotted
  action's `layers[0].strips[0].channelbag(action.slots[0]).fcurves`), or a simple driver of `frame`
  (`frame * 0.2`); put the part's origin at its pivot.  Amplitude must read at scene
  distance (≥ 0.15 rad or ≥ 0.05 m registers in the frame difference).
