## DO / DON'T
- DO use the exact size numbers above; the zone builders and the placement gate rely on them.
- DO make it recognisable as the named thing at scene distance; the description decides its features
  and its condition.
- DO make `variant` (0..n) differ in SILHOUETTE when several copies are placed (the plan's count decides
  how many); a `variant` that only scales is a wasted asset.
- DO give a repeated natural asset colour room — `variant` / `ctx.rng(seed)`-driven colour is one way —
  so many copies do not read as one colour.
- DON'T model a flat plane with a colour where the thing has real thickness (a fence is stakes and
  rails, not a textured quad) — closeups are judged.
- DON'T leave floating pieces: every sub-shape overlaps a neighbour by ≥ 2 mm, and the lowest point
  is exactly z = 0 (the harness measures a part sunk below it or hovering above it).
- DON'T write anything outside the listed file.
